  "topic_en": "Gauss gives a recursion for the quantities ϖ', ϖ'', ϖ''' as a check on a second formula, writes the resulting continued fractions for B^{ix} and B^{x} in terms of ff, and works a logarithmic numerical example for θ = 36°20'.",
  "transcription": "Diese zweite Formel soll eigentlich nur zur Controlle dienen, indem\naus $\\varpi^0$ die folgenden vermittelst der Gleichungen\n$\\varpi' = \\frac{1}{2}\\varpi^0 B^0 \\cos\\theta^2$\n$\\varpi'' = \\frac{3}{4}\\varpi' B' \\cos\\theta^2$\n$\\varpi''' = \\frac{5}{6}\\varpi'' B'' \\cos\\theta^2$ u. s. w.\nabgeleitet werden.\nGeht man hiebei bis $\\varpi^x$, so hat man\n$B^{ix} = \\cfrac{1+ff}{1 - \\cfrac{\\frac{1}{440}ff}{1 - \\cfrac{\\frac{441}{528}ff}{1 - \\cfrac{\\frac{9}{624}ff}{1 - \\cfrac{\\frac{529}{728}ff}{1 - \\cfrac{\\frac{25}{840}ff}{1 - \\frac{625}{960}ff \\text{ etc.}}}}}}}$\n$B^{x} = \\cfrac{1+ff}{1 - \\cfrac{\\frac{1}{528}ff}{1 - \\cfrac{\\frac{529}{624}ff}{1 - \\cfrac{\\frac{9}{728}ff}{1 - \\cfrac{\\frac{625}{840}ff}{1 - \\frac{25}{960}ff \\text{ etc.}}}}}}$\nAls Beispiel setzen wir $\\theta = 36^\\circ 20'$\n\n$\\log\\tan f$ .... 9,8665644.4 | 9,5080750 ... 0,3221625 | $\\log\\frac{1}{2}\\sin 2\\theta$ .... 9,6787858\n$\\log\\tan f^2$ .... 9,7331289 | 8,3866961 | $\\log\\frac{1}{2}\\sin 2\\theta^2$ .... 9,3575716\n$\\log\\frac{729}{1224}$ ....... 9,7749461 | 9,8311256 .... 0,0359394 | $\\log\\frac{361}{360}$ ..... 0,0012047\n$\\log\\frac{49}{1088}$ ....... 8,6535672 | 9,5467377 | $\\log\\frac{289}{288}$ ..... 0,0015053\n$\\log\\frac{625}{960}$ ....... 9,8136088 | 9,9841044 .... 0,3652862[?] | $\\log\\frac{225}{224}$ ..... 0,0019345\n$\\log\\frac{25}{840}$ ....... 8,4736607 | 8,2067896 | $\\log\\frac{169}{168}$ ..... 0,0025774\n$\\log\\frac{529}{728}$ ....... 9,8613243 | 9,8025780 .... 0,0253636 | $\\log\\frac{121}{120}$ ..... 0,0036042\n$\\log\\frac{9}{624}$ ....... 8,1590579 | 9,5944532 | $\\log\\frac{81}{80}$ ..... 0,0053950\n$\\log\\frac{441}{528}$ ....... 9,9218047 | 9,9888426 ..... 0,4032836 | $\\log\\frac{49}{48}$ ..... 0,0089549\n$\\log\\frac{1}{440}$ ....... 7,3565473 | 7,8921868 | $\\log\\frac{25}{24}$ ..... 0,0177288\n | 9,7757680 ..... 0,0130743 | $\\log\\frac{9}{8}$ ..... 0,0511525\n$\\log\\cos\\theta^2$ ....... 9,8122214